     <h1 class="title" title="Chikhaldara Hill Station">Chikhaldara</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/west-india-hill-stations/chilkhaldara-hill-station.jpg" title="Chikhaldara hill station" alt="Chikhaldara hill station, hill stations in india, 

west india hill stations, Chikhaldara" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Amravati district, Maharashtra<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Only Coffee Growing in Maharashtra<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 1118m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 22&#176;C - 35&#176;C, Winter 12&#176;C - 33&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> October to June</p>     
<p><b>Chikhaldhara</b> is the only <b>hill station in the Vidarbha region</b>. It is situated at an altitude of 1,118 m and offers <b>abundant wildlife</b>, beautiful lakes and waterfalls. According to legend, is named after the Chikaldhara Keechaka demon who was killed by the <b>Pandava hero, Bhima</b>. Since this place was called <b>Keechakadara</b>. Over time this has come to be known as Chikhaldara. It is also the region&#39;s coffee growing in Maharashtra and is known for its <b>deep valleys</b> and beauty, making it a <b>popular summer retreat</b>.</p>
